    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1315">

                <pb facs="1451" n="1439" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg1439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860C.01/12–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-12T00:00:00+03:00">December 12,
                            1944—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received December 12—8:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4795. ReEmbs 4777, December 11, 10 p.m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d1315-f1"/> The
                    French Minister<anchor n="26" xml:id="d1315-f2"/> yesterday informed me that
                    Stalin had told de Gaulle that the Polish Lublin Committee would shortly declare
                    itself the Provisional Government of Poland. I assume that the Soviet Government
                    will, of course, then recognize them as such. I have received no information on
                    this from the Soviet Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
